ed plan + draft inputs\n`GET|POST /ai-market/pricing/{product_id}/{capability_id}`  | Quote price for input size\n`POST /ai-market/channel/open` · `close`  | Pre-funded payment channel\n`POST /capabilities/{product_id}/{capability_id}/invoke`  | Invoke; 402 without payment\n`POST /ai-market/pipelines`  | DAG execution + signed bill of materials\n`GET /ai-market/receipt/{nonce}`  | Signed receipt\n`GET /ai-market/stats`  | Live feed (Factory Floor)\n\n## Payment flow (402)\n\n  1. `POST /capabilities/{pid}/{cid}/invoke` → 402 + header `X-Payment-Required` (amount, token, chain, recipient, nonce).\n  2. Client signs on-chain tx or opens a channel: `POST /ai-market/channel/open`.\n  3. Retry with `X-Payment: {\"tx_hash\":\"0x…\"}` or `X-Payment-Channel: ch_…` → 200 + `result`, `receipt`, `continuation`.\n\n## Reference agent (hello world)\n    \n    `python cli/ai_market_agent.py \"translate spec to 5 langs + legal review\" --budget 3.0 \\\n      --base-url https://magic-ai-factory.com\n    `\n\nSDKs (recommended): per-language clients — `pip install aimarket-agent` (Python), `dart pub add aimarket_agent`, `npm install @aimarket/agent`, or the `aimarket-agent` crate (Rust). Guides: `aimarket-sdks/docs/en.md` · `aimarket-agent/docs/en.md`.\n\n> Legacy: `cli/ai_market_sdk.py` (`well_known()`, `manifest_v1()`, `invoke_capability_v1()`) is the pre-v2 factory-internal HTTP client — kept for the factory's own use, not for new integrations.\n\n## Environment\n\nVariable  | Meaning\n--- | ---\n`AIFACTORY_AI_MARKET_CHAIN`  | e.g. `base`\n`AIFACTORY_AI_MARKET_TOKEN`  | e.g. `USDT`\n`AIFACTORY_AI_MARKET_CONTRACT`  | Pilot contract (optional)\n`AIFACTORY_AI_MARKET_DEMO_PAYMENT`  | `1` = accept `demo-*` tx (dev/demo)\n`AIFACTORY_PUBLIC_URL`  | Canonical URLs in manifests\n\n## Admin: Factory Floor\n\nAdmin → Factory Floor shows node 🤖 External AI and recent AI Market spend when external agents invoke capabilities (`/ai-market/stats`).\n\n## Roadmap\n\nPhase  | Content\n--- | ---\n0  | v0 discovery + settlement\n1–4  | v1 schema, 402, channels, pipelines, reference agent\n5  | Factory Floor live feed\n6  | Federation (crawl foreign manifests) — TBD--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/aimarket-hub/tree)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     | [aimarket-protocol](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol/tree/main/) | Normative v2 spec |\n\nImage: alexar76\n\n## AIMarket\n\nFavorite\n\nAI & Machine LearningPayments & BillingAgent Orchestration\n\nby alexar76\n\nOverviewSchemaSourceRelated ServersDiscussionsAdmin\n\nPython\n\nHybrid\n\n  * aimarket-hub\n\n  * aimarket_hub\n\nREADME.md\n    \n    `<!-- aicom-mirror-notice -->\n    > **🔄 Synced from a monorepo — but with a live history.** `aimarket-hub` mirrors the\n    > canonical AI-Factory monorepo. History here is append-only (no force-push).\n    > **Pull requests are welcome** — merged PRs are imported back into the monorepo\n    > and re-synced here, so your contribution becomes canonical.\n    > 💬 **[Issues](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues)** · **[Pull requests](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pulls)** both welcome.\n    \n    # AIMarket Hub\n    \n    <!-- aicom-readme-badges -->\n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/ci.svg\" alt=\"CI\" /></a>\n    | `GET` | `/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json` | MCP server card (SEP-1649 / Smithery fallback) |\n    | `GET` | `/llms.txt` | Short agent-readable Hub + MCP door |\n    | `GET` / `POST` | `/mcp` | Hosted MCP — GET info; POST Streamable-HTTP (`market_search`, `market_invoke`) |\n    | `GET` | `/.well-known/agent-card.json` | A2A 1.0 Agent Card (cacheable + ETag) |\n    | `POST` | `/a2a` | A2A 1.0 JSON-RPC: marketplace search, paid invoke as Tasks, `GetTask`/`ListTasks`/`CancelTask` ([docs/a2a.md](docs/a2a.md)) |\n    | `GET` | `/ai-market/v2/manifest` | Hybrid Ed25519 + ML-DSA-65 capability catalog when PQC is enabled |\n    | `GET` | `/ai-market/v2/search` | NL federated search (`intent`, `budget`, `category`) |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/supply/stake` | Deposit publisher stake (unlock community publish) |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/supply/register` | Publish community capability + `invoke_url` |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/invoke` | Invoke capability (plugin hooks, safety gate) |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/receipts/verify` | Verify a receipt against this Hub's pinned live Ed25519 + ML-DSA-65 identities |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/channel/open` | Open pre-funded payment channel |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/channel/close` | Close channel — settle + refund remainder |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/federation/announce` | Peer hub announcement |\n    | `GET` | `/ai-market/v2/federation/peers` | Known peers + trust scores + pin status (`key_mismatch`) |\n    | `GET` | `/ai-market/v2/federation/assay` | Last sandbox scorecard (`pass` auto-admits by default) |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/federation/assay` | Admin: re-run SSRF / signature / sandbox assay |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/federation/crawl` | Trigger BFS crawl of seed peers |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/federation/peers/approve` | Admin: toggle peer `trusted` (anti-TOFU) |\n    | `POST` | `/ai-market/v2/federation/peers/repin` | Admin: rotate a sticky peer pin after legitimate key change |\n    | `GET` | `/ai-market/v2/plugins` | Loaded plugin catalog |\n    | `GET` | `/ai-market/v2/reputation/{hub_url}` | Trust score breakdown |\n    | `GET` | `/ai-market/v2/stats/live` | Real-time invocation feed |\n    \n    **Authorization.** Self-service publishers use their own `X-API-Key` on\n      redeeming needs `X-Payment-Secret`: once the payment is mined its nonce and hash are\n      public, and the secret is what shows the redeemer is the one who paid. Only the\n      transfer the buyer's own authorization moved pays for the call. `payTo` on the\n      402 and in the Bazaar index is the **seller**, not the platform wallet.\n    \n    An operator may take a share of a catalogue sale **without** taking custody of it:\n    `AIMARKET_MARKET_FEE_BPS` plus a deployed\n    [`MarketSplitter`](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/contracts/evm/src/MarketSplitter.sol) makes the 402 name a\n    contract that forwards both shares in the buyer's own transaction. The hub then\n    requires both `Transfer` legs — seller and operator — rather than trusting that the\n    payment was routed through any particular address. Off by default.\n    \n    **Where the money goes, rail by rail, with diagrams:\n    [`docs/money-rails.md`](docs/money-rails.md).**\n    \n    See [`aimarket_hub/settle.py`](aimarket_hub/settle.py) and [`aimarket_hub/x402.py`](aimarket_hub/x402.py).\n    \n    ### ERC-8004 identity\n    \n    The public hub at modelmarket.dev is ERC-8004 agent\n    [`96682` on Base](https://8004scan.io/agents/base/96682), registered on 2026-10-01 in the\n    canonical IdentityRegistry `0x8004A169…a432` and owned by the operator wallet\n    `0x1218ff36…Ad0a`. The hub names that agentId in the `erc8004` block of its signed\n    `/.well-known/ai-market.json` and marks it self-declared (`verified_by_this_hub: false`), so a\n    reader confirms it against the registry. Another operator registers from their own wallet, then\n    sets `AIMARKET_ERC8004_AGENT_ID` (plus `_CHAIN`, `_NETWORK`, `_AGENT_URI`). Transactions,\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAIMarket MCP Packager - Odel Module Marketplace (https://odel.app/modules/alexar76/aimarket-plugins)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;   * Docs: https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-plugins/blob/main/docs/install.md\n## Demo\n\n  * Live: https://modelmarket.dev/plugins/demo\n  * Docs: https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-plugins/blob/main/docs/install.md\n\n## Related repos\n\nRepo  | Role\n--- | ---\naimarket-hub  | Loads plugins at invoke time\noracles  | Verifiable math capabilities (separate repo)\naicom  | AI-Factory monorepo\ndioscuri  | Twin community agents — MNEMOSYNE Q&A\n\n## Community\n\nThe DIOSCURI twins answer questions from synced GitHub docs.\n\nChannel  | Twin  | Best for\n--- | --- | ---\nDiscord  | Pollux  | Help, ideas, show-and-tell\nTelegram  | Castor  | Releases, digests, quick news\n\nEcosystem map: Alien Monitor · AICOM\n\n## Checked by Odel\n\n  * Registry verified the namespace io.github.alexar76\n  * Repository reachable, not archived\n\n### Assessed by AI Jev\n\nHarmful\n    \n    7%\nFirst-party\n    \n    84%\nHigh impact\n    \n    15%\nAdult content\n    \n    1%\n\nRead from the listing and README on 10 Oct 2026. AI can make mistakes: a guide, not a check.\n\n## Requirements\n\nRuns\n    On your machine\n\nSign-in\n    PyPI\n\nCredentials\n    None asked\n\nClients\n    Any MCP client\n\n  * aimarket-mcp-packager@2.0.1 pypi 43 a week\n\n## Details\n\nVersion\n    2.0.1\n\nUpdated\n    8 Oct 2026\n\nRepo created\n    22 May 2026\n\nLicense\n    MIT\n\nLanguage\n    Python\n\nGitHub\n    1 stars · 0 forks · 0 issues\n\nRegistry name\n    io.github.alexar76/aimarket-plugins\n\n  * alexar76/aimarket-plugins\n\n## Tags\n\n  * Self-hosting & homelab\n  * MCP gateways & tool hubs\n  * Agent collaboration--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nattested-memory · PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/attested-memory/)\nciteturn2search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Source: alexar76/attested-memory (`clients/python`).\n    unit = client.write(\"Supplier terms\", \"Net 30\", tags=[\"finance\"])\n    client.read(unit[\"id\"])               # raises IntegrityError if the text does not match its hash\n    \n\nWhat is checked where:\n\n | where\n--- | ---\nyour identity (`did:actor:` + SHA-256 of your public key) and a one-time signed proof per request  | client signs, server verifies\nthe text of a memory matches its `content_hash`  | this client\n`truth` (supported / contested / rejected) and `provenance` (attested receipt)  | reported by the hub\n\nThe proof is a signature over `<actor id>\\n<unix seconds>\\n<nonce>`: good for five minutes and one request, so a captured header set replays nowhere.\n\nEnvironment for the CLI: `ATTESTED_MEMORY_HOME`, `ATTESTED_MEMORY_URL`, `ATTESTED_MEMORY_API_KEY`.\n\nApache-2.0. Source: alexar76/attested-memory (`clients/python`).\n\n## Project links\n\n  * Homepage\n  * Source\n\n## Key dates\n\nPyPI data\n\nData sourced directly from PyPI's database.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMetis - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki/Metis)\nciteturn2search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; > Live demo: metis.modelmarket.dev · 3D landing: alexar76.github.io/metis · Source: github.com/alexar76/metis · PyPI: `aimarket-metis` · Factory integration: `docs/metis-integration.md`\n\n# Metis - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki\n\n# Metis — cognition & verification tier\n\nMetis (μῆτις) is the ecosystem's distributed cognitive layer over any LLM — Understanding Council → fail-closed confidence gate → layered Mixture-of-Agents → grounded verifier. It returns a machine-readable verification envelope (`verify_score`, `verified`, optional `needs_clarification`).\n\n> Live demo: metis.modelmarket.dev · 3D landing: alexar76.github.io/metis · Source: github.com/alexar76/metis · PyPI: `aimarket-metis` · Factory integration: `docs/metis-integration.md`\n\n## Why Metis matters in AICOM\n\nLayer  | Role\n--- | ---\nOracles  | Verifiable math primitives (randomness, VDF, reputation, …)\nMetis  | Verifiable cognition — multi-agent reasoning + confidence gate on natural-language decisions\nAI-Factory  | Produces products; optionally calls Metis on high-stakes stages (`architect`, `methodologist`)\nARGUS  | Demand-side agent; can consume Metis + MCP tools like any other host\n\nHard invariant: factory and Metis are independent. Missing Metis → factory runs unchanged (fail-open gate). Missing factory → Metis serves `/v1/*` normally.\n\n## Factory integration (optional gate)\n\nHigh-stakes pipeline stages can POST to Metis `/v1/verify` via `llm/metis_gate.py` (HTTP only — never imports `metis`).\n    \n    `export METIS_URL=https://metis.internal:8080   # default http://127.0.0.1:8080\n    export AIFACTORY_METIS_GATE=auto               # auto | on | off (default auto)\n    export AIFACTORY_METIS_GATE_BLOCK=0          # 1 = allow low-confidence to escalate\n    `\n\nFull env table + sequence diagrams: `docs/metis-integration.md` · RU · ES · FR · ZH\n\n## MCP tools (Metis as consumer)\n\nMetis agents can attach ecosystem MCP servers via presets:\n\nPreset  | Server  | Tools\n--- | --- | ---\n`aimarket-oracle-gateway`  | aimarket-oracle-gateway  | 35 verifiable oracle tools\n`aimarket-web`  | aimarket-mcp  | `web_fetch`, `web_search`, `metis_verify` (SSRF-hardened)\n    \n    `enable_mcp_tools: true\n    mcp_ecosystem_presets:\n      - aimarket-oracle-gateway\n      - aimarket-web\n    `\n\naimarket-mcp — shared MCP gateway (stdio on Glama, HTTP self-host). Written once; consumed by Metis, ARGUS, and any stdio/HTTP MCP host.\n\nMetis-side doc: `metis/docs/en/ECOSYSTEM.md`\n\n## Alien Monitor\n\nMetis appears as the `cognition` node in Alien Monitor — live stats + in-graph chat proxied server-side (`POST /api/metis/chat`) so API keys never reach the browser.\n\n## Quick start (standalone)\n    \n    `git clone https://github.com/alexar76/metis.git && cd metis\n    pip install -e \".[dev,distributed]\"\n    metis-serve --port 8080\n    # OpenAPI: /v1/verify · /v1/chat/completions · /aimarket/invoke\n    `\n\nDocker: `docker compose up -d` in the metis repo.--------------------------------