 that page.\n\nSettlement in the pull request goes through the CDP facilitator. That is a payment rail for those six URLs. It is not a claim that the Hub homepage is a busy market.\n\n## The on-chain IDs are published. The awesome-list is not.\n\nmodelmarket.dev/.well-known/agent-registration.json names three agents on Base, registry `eip155:8453:0x8004A169FB4a3325136EB29fA0ceB6D2e539a432`:\n\n  * AIMarket Hub — agent 96682\n  * HISTOR — agent 96683\n  * WARDEN — agent 96684\n\nThe awesome-erc8004 pull request is a README link to those IDs. Merging it changes a list. It does not create the agents. Leaving it open does not delete them either. A scan link from the pull request: 8004scan.io/agents/base/96682.\n\n## What I will not say until a maintainer clicks merge\n\n  * WARDEN is not in the Docker MCP catalog yet.\n  * The Hub is not in that catalog yet.\n  * AIMarket is not on the x402 ecosystem page yet.\n  * The three names are not in awesome-erc8004 yet.\n  * Cline has a submission issue, not a marketplace card.\n\nThe useful check is the thing you can call: the npm package, the MCP URL, the a2mcp list, the registration file. The catalogs are a paper trail. This week the paper is still in review.\n\n⭐ github.com/alexar76/warden · github.com/alexar76/histor · github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nI opened a live agent marketplace. The receipts were the product. - DEV Community (https://dev.to/alexar76/i-opened-a-live-agent-marketplace-the-receipts-were-the-product-4hl1)\nciteturn2search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; Code: github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub (MIT)\n\nAlex\n\nPosted on Sep 15 • Originally published at modelmarket.dev\n\n# I opened a live agent marketplace. The receipts were the product.\n\n#ai #opensource #showdev #webdev\n\nMost “agent economy” posts sell you a framework, a Discord, or a token.\n\nI wanted the boring thing: a public catalog where an agent can find a tool, call it, and keep a receipt — without me standing in the loop.\n\nThat surface is live. It is called AIMarket Hub. The URL is modelmarket.dev. Crypto stays off this title on purpose. The shape here is discover → invoke → receipt.\n\nCounted 2026-09-15 from `/ai-market/v2/stats/live`:\n\n | \n--- | ---\nInvokes  | 710 (704 ok — 99.2%)\nExternal / self  | 700 / 10\nFederated hubs  | 14\nCapabilities  | 177\np50 latency (24h)  | 90 ms\nRevenue / hour  | $0.0010\n\nThat last number is the honesty tax. This is not Uniswap. It is a small live market that already meters calls. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nalexar76 - MCP Server (https://mcprepository.com/alexar76)\nciteturn2search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Image: alexar76 ... MCP server: verifiable oracle services (Platon VRF, Chronos VDF, LUMEN reputation) for AI agents — pay-per-call over the AIMarket protocol, every result independently verifiable.\n\nImage: alexar76\n\n# alexar76\n\n5 MCP Server\n\nMPC Server by alexar76\n\nImage: icon\n\naimarket-mcp — ecosystem MCP gateway\n\nalexar76\n\n»aimarket-mcp\n\nEcosystem MCP gateway — web fetch/search + Metis verify behind one SSRF-hardened MCP endpoint (Streamable-HTTP). Consumed by Metis and ARGUS via the aimarket-web preset.\n\nOct 8, 2026\n\n1 stars\n\nImage: icon\n\nARGUS-3 — MCP server\n\nalexar76\n\n»argus\n\nARGUS-3 — wallet-native, security-hardened personal agent; demand-side reference client and the reference host for the WARDEN MCP firewall (@aimarket/warden, a separate package) plus native AIMarket consumer/provider. Owner-locked Telegram, multi-provider, autonomous offline.\n\nOct 8, 2026\n\n1 stars\n\nImage: icon\n\naimarket-mcp-packager — MCP server\n\nalexar76\n\n»aimarket-plugins\n\nAI Market Plugins — 14 plugin packages (auction, channels, data-cap, dataset, mcp-packager, nft, orchestrator, personas, promo, reputation, safety, streaming, tee, zk)\n\nMay 24, 2026\n\n0 stars\n\nImage: icon\n\naimarket-oracle-gateway — MCP server\n\nalexar76\n\n»aimarket-oracle-gateway\n\nMCP server: verifiable oracle services (Platon VRF, Chronos VDF, LUMEN reputation) for AI agents — pay-per-call over the AIMarket protocol, every result independently verifiable.\n\nOct 8, 2026\n\n0 stars\n\nImage: icon\n\nWARDEN — MCP server\n\nalexar76\n\n»warden\n\nWARDEN — MCP security firewall: vets an MCP server's tool definitions against static-scan rules, a signed threat feed, origin and tool-def pinning before any tool reaches the model. Zero-dependency TypeScript library.\n\nOct 8, 2026\n\n0 stars--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\naimarket-mcp MCP server · io.github.alexar76 · ProtocolProbe (https://protocolprobe.com/mcp/servers/io.github.alexar76/aimarket-mcp)\nciteturn2search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; io.github.alexar76/aimarket-mcp is a remote and local MCP server listed in the official MCP registry at version 0.6.4, under the namespace of the GitHub account alexar76.\n\nMCP servers › io.github.alexar76 › aimarket-mcp\n\nMCP server · registry snapshot 2026-10-30 · last tested 2026-10-30\n\n# io.github.alexar76/aimarket-mcp\n\nAIMarket MCP Gateway — the publisher's title\n\nby alexar76 · GitHub account (the registry's namespace rule)repository: same ownerSource ↗PyPI ↗\n\nStdio + HTTP MCP gateway: SSRF-hardened web_fetch, web_search, metis_verify, market_search. — the publisher's description\n\n8 of 8 record checks metTopic: search-and-web-data · AI-classified version 0.6.4 Python MIT standard input/output, streamable HTTP\n\n## Summary\n\nio.github.alexar76/aimarket-mcp is a remote and local MCP server listed in the official MCP registry at version 0.6.4, under the namespace of the GitHub account alexar76. Its linked repository, github.com/alexar76/aimarket-mcp, belongs to the same GitHub account.\n\n### Record checks\n\n8 of 8 record checks met · 1 does not apply\n"
